},{"text":"மரம்","lemma":"மரம்","gloss":"tree"}],"gloss":"guardian tree"},{"surface":"தடிதல்","parts":[{"text":"தடி","lemma":"தடிதல்","gloss":"cut"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"தல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"cutting down"},{"surface":"ஓம்பு","parts":[{"text":"ஓம்பு","lemma":"ஓம்புதல்","gloss":"refrain/protect"}],"gloss":"refrain from"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெடுதல்","parts":[{"text":"நெடு","lemma":"நெடுமை","gloss":"tall"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"தல்","gloss":"suffix"}],"gloss":"tall"},{"surface":"யானைக்குக்","parts":[{"text":"யானைக்குக்","lemma":"யானைக்குக்","gloss":"to the elephants"}],"gloss":"to the elephants","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கந்தாற்றாவே","parts":[{"text":"கந்து","lemma":"கந்து","gloss":"tying post"},{"text":"ஆற்றாவே","lemma":"ஆற்றல்","gloss":"they are capable / they bear"}],"gloss":"they serve as tying posts"}]}],"literal":"Whether they are experts or whether they are novices / to those who approach to praise, like the dark-hued deity (Vishnu) / O Maṟa of highly praised excellence and famous glory! / I have one thing to say to you, if you ask what it is: / When you yourself capture the country of others, in their country, / let your young soldiers seize the fields with drooping ears of grain, / let fire also destroy the wide big towns, / even if you destroy the enemies with your long spear that glitters and shines like rising lightning, / refrain from cutting down even a little bit of their guardian trees, / for your tall elephants, they serve as tying posts!","translation":"Whether they are experts or novices, to all who come to praise you, you are like the dark-hued Lord Vishnu, O Maṟa of highly praised excellence and famous glory! I have one thing to say to you, if you ask what it is: When you conquer the lands of your enemies, let your young soldiers plunder their fields of drooping grain; let fire consume their wide, grand towns; and let your long, glittering spear, flashing like lightning, destroy your foes. But refrain from cutting down their sacred guardian trees, for they are the only posts strong enough to tether your majestic, tall elephants!","modern":"பாடிப் புகழத் தெரிந்த அறிஞர்களாயினும், தெரியாத எளியவர்களாயினும், தன்னை நாடி வருபவர்களுக்குக் காக்கும் கடவுளாகிய திருமால் போன்றவனே! மிகுந்த சிறப்பும் புகழும் கொண்ட மாறனே! உன்னிடம் நான் ஒன்று கூற விரும்புகிறேன், அது என்னவென்றால்: நீ பகைவர்களின் நாட்டைப் போரிட்டுக் கைப்பற்றும் போது, அவர்களுடைய வளைந்த கதிர்களைக் கொண்ட வயல்களை உன்னுடைய இளம் வீரர்கள் கொள்ளையடிக்கட்டும்; அவர்களுடைய அகன்ற பெரிய ஊர்களைத் தீக்கிரையாக்கட்டும்; மின்னலைப் போல ஒளிரும் உனது நீண்ட வேல் பகைவர்களை அழிப்பதாக இருந்தாலும் அழிக்கட்டும்; ஆனால், அவர்களுடைய காவல் மரங்களை மட்டும் வெட்டாமல் தடுத்துக் காப்பாற்றுவாயாக! ஏனெனில், உன்னுடைய உயர்ந்த யானைகளைக் கட்டுவதற்கு அந்த மரங்களே தகுந்த தூண்களாக விளங்கும்!","explanation":"The poet Kāviripūmpaṭṭiṉattu Kārikkaṇṇaṉār addresses the Pandyan king Ilavantihaip Paḷḷit Tuñciya Naṉmāṟaṉ in this Vañci (conquest) poem. He praises the king's boundless generosity, comparing him to Lord Vishnu (Māyōṉ) who protects all who approach him, regardless of their skill. The poet then advises the king that while he may plunder the enemy's fields, burn their towns, and slay their warriors with his lightning-like spear, he must spare their sacred guardian trees (kaṭimaram). This advice is framed as a clever compliment: these massive trees are the only posts strong enough to tether the king's own victorious, towering war elephants. This image beautifully blends the ferocity of war with the ultimate triumph of the conqueror.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.7],[0.7,1.0],[1.0,1.5],[1.5,2.39],[2.61,3.5],[3.5,4.0],[4.0,4.1],[4.1,5.3],[5.3,5.4],[5.4,6.1],[6.1,6.4],[6.54,7.7],[7.7,8.3],[8.3,8.7],[8.81,9.5],[9.5,10.1],[10.21,10.67],[10.9,11.5],[11.5,11.9],[11.9,12.2],[12.2,13.1],[13.1,13.4],[13.4,13.99],[14.03,14.68],[14.68,14.84],[15.0,15.9],[1